ggml-cpu: 16-row interleaved AVX512-VNNI GEMM for Q8_0 / Q4_0 / IQ4_NL weights at batch >= 32, adapted from
ik_llama.cpp's Q8_0_R16 kernels (#2764, #2807; MIT).
On builds with AVX512F + BW + VL + VNNI (the cascadelake / icelake / zen4 / sapphirerapids CPU variants) a mul_mat with
Q8_0, Q4_0 or IQ4_NL weights, at least 32 activation rows and a multiple of 16 weight rows now runs here instead of
the 8-column legacy tiled GEMM (legacy-q8.cpp, ymm VPDPBUSD) or tinyBLAS. Each thread converts 32 weight rows at a
time into 16-row interleaved blocks (the integer values + 128 as unsigned bytes, the fp16 block scales widened to f32)
in a per-thread buffer, and one zmm VPDPBUSD multiplies 4 bytes of 16 weight rows with one activation code word. The
activation scales and code sums (which cancel the +128) are computed once per mul_mat into the work buffer.
The integer product of every 32-block is the one vec_dot forms and the float sum over blocks runs in the same order
as the legacy tiled GEMM, so renders match the legacy path bit for bit. Other types, other CPU variants and smaller
batches are unchanged. GGML_CPU_Q80_R16=0 turns it off, or a comma list of type names limits it.
Colab L4 VM CPU (Xeon @ 2.20 GHz, Cascade Lake, 6 cores): Q8_0 / Q4_0 / IQ4_NL mul_mat 1.4-1.7x; Z-Image Turbo Q8_0
512 px 4 steps sampling 86.96 -> 62.42 s (1.39x), FLUX.2 klein 4B Q4_0 68.22 -> 47.21 s (1.44x), Q4_K / Q6_K unchanged.
Renders are pixel-identical with GGML_CPU_Q80_R16=0 (max abs 0). Checked out of tree against a double-precision
reference for the three types (batch tails, thread splits inside a unit, a broadcast batch dimension, both fallbacks).

